    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Description\n\nSuppose I have the following text:\n\n`clever Crafty camels`\n\nCurrently, doing a single_character jump to \"c\" offers 2 jump spots.  With smartcase enabled, it seems as if the uppercase C should also be offered.  Is this possible?",
